It works by intercepting the `X-Cookie` HTTP header sent by a browser and modifying the data before it reaches the server. When a page loads cookies, Stop-Cookie.js checks the incoming header against its internal database of cookies. If it finds a match, it sets the new cookie value to the one stored in the database, effectively hiding the fact that the cookie came from the user's machine.

