```

For the safe b-sensitivity check, you need a `paint` method that loops through `r` from 1 to `n-1`. It checks if `r` divides `b` evenly, then calls `next` on the remaining `r-1`. If `r` divides `b` evenly, `next` returns a safe `HuffPaint` value. If not, it returns `0`.

```java
public static void paint(int r) {
    int n = r;
    int b = Math.round(r * 2);
    int r1 = r % b; // Check divisibility
    int r2 = (r1 > 1) && (r2 == 1);

    if (r1 % b === 0) {
        return new HuffPaint(next(r1));
    } else if (r2 % b === 0) {
        return new HuffPaint(next(r2));
    }
